iti83:5.2 | S: “Sir, what do the gods reckon to be going to a good place? | T: “What, lord, is the devas’ reckoning of going to a good destination?
iti83:6.1 | S: What do they reckon to be blessed with good fortune? | T: What is their reckoning of the gain that is good to gain?
iti83:7.1 | S: What do they reckon to become well grounded?” | T: What is their reckoning of becoming well-established?”
iti83:8.1 | S: “It is human existence, mendicant, that the gods reckon to be going to a good place. | T: “The human state, monks, is the devas’ reckoning of going to a good destination.
iti83:9.1 | S: When a human being gains faith in the teaching and training proclaimed by the Realized One, | T: Having become a human being, acquiring conviction in the Dhamma-&-Vinaya taught by the Tathāgata:
iti83:9.2 | S: that is what the gods reckon to be blessed with good fortune. | T: this is the devas’ reckoning of the gain that is good to gain.
iti83:10.1 | S: When that faith in the Realized One is settled, rooted, and planted deep; when it’s strong and can’t be shifted by any ascetic or brahmin or god or Māra or divinity or by anyone in the world, | T: When that conviction is settled within one–rooted, established, & strong, not to be destroyed by any brahman or contemplative; deva, Māra, or Brahma; or anyone else in the world:
iti83:10.2 | S: that is what the gods reckon to become well grounded.” | T: this is the devas’ reckoning of becoming well-established.”
