## snp5.4
snp5.4:1.1 | S: “To the imperturbable, the seer of the root,” | T: To the one unperturbed, who has seen the roots,
snp5.4:1.2 | S: said Venerable Puṇṇaka, | T: (none)
snp5.4:1.3 | S: “I have come seeking with a question. | T: I have come with a question.
snp5.4:1.4 | S: On what grounds have seers and men, | T: Because of what have many human seers
snp5.4:1.5 | S: aristocrats and brahmins here in the world | T: —noble warriors, brahmans—
snp5.4:1.6 | S: performed so many different <j>sacrifices to the gods? | T: offered sacrifices to devas here in the world?
snp5.4:1.7 | S: I ask you, Blessed One; please tell me this.” | T: I ask you, Blessed One. Please tell me.
snp5.4:2.1 | S: “Whatever seers and men,” | T: The Buddha: Those many human seers
snp5.4:2.2 | S: replied the Buddha, | T: (none)
snp5.4:2.3 | S: “aristocrats and brahmins here in the world | T: —noble warriors, brahmans—
snp5.4:2.4 | S: have performed so many different <j>sacrifices to the gods: | T: who have offered sacrifices to devas here in the world,
snp5.4:2.5 | S: all performed sacrifices bound to old age, | T: Puṇṇaka, hoping for more of this state of being, offered their sacrifices
snp5.4:2.6 | S: longing for this place.” | T: because of aging.
snp5.4:3.1 | S: “As to those seers and men,” | T: Puṇṇaka: These many human seers
snp5.4:3.2 | S: said Venerable Puṇṇaka, | T: (none)
snp5.4:3.3 | S: “and aristocrats and brahmins here in the world | T: —noble warriors, brahmans—
snp5.4:3.4 | S: who have performed so many different <j>sacrifices to the gods: | T: who have offered sacrifices to devas here in the world:
snp5.4:3.5 | S: being diligent in the technique of sacrifice, | T: Have they, Blessed One, heeding the path of sacrifice,
snp5.4:3.6 | S: have they crossed over rebirth and old age, good fellow? | T: dear sir, crossed over birth & aging?
snp5.4:3.7 | S: I ask you, Blessed One; please tell me this.” | T: I ask you, Blessed One. Please tell me.
snp5.4:4.1 | S: “Hoping, invoking, praying, and worshiping,” | T: The Buddha: They hoped for, liked, longed for, so they sacrificed—
snp5.4:4.2 | S: replied the Buddha, | T: (none)
snp5.4:4.3 | S: “they pray for pleasure derived from profit. | T: they longed for sensuality, dependent on gain.
snp5.4:4.4 | S: Devoted to sacrifice, besotted by rebirth, | T: I tell you: Those who take on the yoke of sacrifice, impassioned with the passion for becoming,
snp5.4:4.5 | S: they’ve not crossed over rebirth and old age, <j>I declare.” | T: have not crossed over birth & aging.
snp5.4:5.1 | S: “If those devoted to sacrifice,” | T: Puṇṇaka: If those who take on the yoke of sacrifice
snp5.4:5.2 | S: said Venerable Puṇṇaka, | T: (none)
snp5.4:5.3 | S: “have not, by sacrificing, <j>crossed over rebirth and old age, | T: haven’t crossed over birth & aging,
snp5.4:5.4 | S: who then in the world of gods and humans | T: then who in the world, dear sir, of beings divine & human
snp5.4:5.5 | S: has crossed over rebirth and old age, good fellow? | T: has crossed over birth & aging?
snp5.4:5.6 | S: I ask you, Blessed One; please tell me this.” | T: I ask you, Blessed One. Please tell me.
snp5.4:6.1 | S: “Having appraised the world high and low,” | T: The Buddha: He who has fathomed the high & low in the world,
snp5.4:6.2 | S: replied the Buddha, | T: (none)
snp5.4:6.3 | S: “there is nothing in the world that disturbs them. | T: for whom there is nothing perturbing in the world—
snp5.4:6.4 | S: Peaceful, unclouded, untroubled, <j>with no need for hope— | T: evaporated, undesiring, untroubled, at peace—
snp5.4:6.5 | S: they’ve crossed over rebirth and old age, I declare.” | T: he, I tell you, has crossed over birth & aging.
snp5.4:6.6 | P: Puṇṇakamāṇavapucchā tatiyā. | T: (none)

## snp5.6
snp5.6:1.1 | S: “I ask you, Blessed One; please tell me this,” | T: I ask you, Blessed One. Please tell me.
snp5.6:1.2 | S: said Venerable Dhotaka, | T: (none)
snp5.6:1.3 | S: “I long for your voice, great seer. | T: I hope for your words, Great Seer.
snp5.6:1.4 | S: After hearing your message, | T: Having heard your pronouncement,
snp5.6:1.5 | S: I shall train myself for extinguishment.” | T: I’ll train for my own unbinding.
snp5.6:2.1 | S: “Well then, be keen, alert,” | T: The Buddha: In that case, be ardent—
snp5.6:2.2 | S: replied the Buddha, | T: (none)
snp5.6:2.3 | S: “and mindful right here. | T: astute & mindful right here.
snp5.6:2.4 | S: After hearing this message, go on | T: Then, having heard my pronouncement,
snp5.6:2.5 | S: and train yourself for extinguishment.” | T: train for your own unbinding.
snp5.6:3.1 | S: “I see in the world of gods and humans | T: Dhotaka: I see in the world of beings divine & human,
